course: dictionary
lesson: 7041
title: Pas: a word that is not quite English
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Pas» is a French word, so you will not find it as an ordinary English word. You will meet it in French sentences and in a few English phrases borrowed from French, such as «a faux pas».
explain: In French, «pas» means «not». It works with «ne» to make a sentence negative: «je ne sais pas» means «I don't know». In casual French people often just say «pas» on its own, and to an English ear it sounds like «pah».
explain: In ballet, «pas» means a step. A «pas de deux» is a dance for two people. In everyday English, «a faux pas» is an embarrassing social mistake, like saying the wrong thing at a party. It comes from French and means «false step».
fact: «Pas» means «not» in French, and it often works with «ne», as in «je ne comprends pas» (I don't understand).
fact: «Ce n'est pas grave» means «It's not a big deal» in French.
fact: In ballet, «pas» means a step, so a «pas de deux» is a dance for two.
fact: «A faux pas» is an embarrassing social mistake, and it comes from French meaning «false step».
fact: Saying «Je ne comprends pas» is smart, because it tells people you need help understanding.
exercise: In «je ne comprends pas», what does «pas» mean? | Yes | *Not | A dance step | A kind of cake
exercise: In ballet, what is a «pas de deux»? | A rude word | A long walk | A cup of tea | *A dance for two people
exercise: «A faux pas» is best described as: | *An embarrassing social mistake | A long journey | A kind of soup | A ballet teacher
test: Which French phrase means «It's not a big deal»? | Bonjour, merci | Je m'appelle Sam | *Ce n'est pas grave | Au revoir, à bientôt
test: Literally, what does «faux pas» mean? | Big meal | Long walk | Good step | *False step
exam: Which word in French makes a sentence negative, as in «je ne sais pas»? | Bonjour | Chat | *Pas | Lune
